<protocol name="visual_quality" type="shared" domain="visual">

## PURPOSE

Single source of truth for visual quality standards.
What makes professional output. When to ship vs iterate.

---

## THE PHOTOREALISM IMPERATIVE

**Every output must be indistinguishable from professional photography.**

| Authentic | Fake (NEVER) |
|-----------|--------------|
| Natural light falloff | Flat, even lighting |
| Real shadows grounding product | Floating, no contact shadow |
| Material-accurate surfaces | Plastic/CGI look |
| Believable context | Awkward placement |
| Natural colors | Over-saturated, HDR |
| Subtle imperfection | Uncanny perfection |

**Test**: Would a professional photographer believe this is real?

---

## QUALITY DIMENSIONS

| Dimension | What to Evaluate |
|-----------|------------------|
| **Composition** | Product dominance, intentional negative space, framing |
| **Lighting** | Reveals form, shadow quality, specular control |
| **Material** | Surface reads true, texture visible, reflections correct |
| **Edges** | Surgical extraction, no halos/fringing/artifacts |
| **Photorealism** | Grounded, shadows, looks shot not rendered |

---

## SCORING

| Score | Level | Action |
|-------|-------|--------|
| 9-10 | Exceptional | Ship with confidence |
| 8-8.9 | Professional | Ship |
| 7-7.9 | Acceptable | Consider iterating |
| <7 | Below standard | Must iterate or escalate |

**Ship threshold**: ALL dimensions 8+ AND photorealism checklist passes.

---

## PHOTOREALISM CHECKLIST

Before shipping ANY image:

```
[ ] Contact shadow present? (product touches surface)
[ ] Lighting direction consistent?
[ ] Materials render true to nature?
[ ] Product scale correct for context?
[ ] Colors natural, not over-processed?
[ ] No AI artifacts? (weird edges, texture repetition)
[ ] Would fool a professional photographer?
```

**Any check fails = iterate before shipping.**

---

## FIDELITY VS CREATIVITY

| Zone | Rule |
|------|------|
| **Fidelity (NO changes)** | Colors, artwork, text, shape, texture |
| **Enhancement (YES changes)** | Background, lighting quality, sharpness, composition |

**Fix photography problems. Never change product identity.**

When processing source products:
- Color cast from bad lighting -> FIX (correct to true colors)
- Blur -> FIX (sharpen)
- Product's actual color -> PRESERVE (never shift)
- Product's artwork/labels -> PRESERVE (same design, sharper)

---

## COMMON FAILURES

| Failure | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| "Technically correct, emotionally dead" | No creative vision | Ask "what makes this product SPECIAL?" |
| "Over-processed uncanny valley" | Enhancement too aggressive | Reduce, let imperfections remain |
| "Generic studio shot" | Same treatment for everything | Let product character guide approach |
| "Floating product" | Missing contact shadow | Add proper grounding shadow |
| "CGI look" | Too perfect, wrong materials | Add subtle imperfection, fix material rendering |

---

## SELF-CRITIQUE

After generating, ask:

1. **Identity**: Same product, just better photographed?
2. **Sharpness**: Tack sharp on product features?
3. **Photorealism**: Grounded, shadowed, looks real?
4. **Emotion**: Creates desire for the product?
5. **Dimensions**: All 8+?

**All yes = SHIP. Any no = ITERATE.**

